---
import SiteLayout from '../../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/about.css';

const home = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<SiteLayout
  title="About Study Hub | Learning Resources for Ugandan Students"
  description="Learn how Study Hub helps learners find subject resources, study notes, exam practice, and practical tools for focused revision."
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <meta name="google-site-verification" content="sfHZ25XlkVnxKqIxzyH05-ZSdGWMMvXok7V3de4N0PY" />
    <meta name="google-site-verification" content="ekOqLM1fntpBVAn7Ey_2SjgOF9qNX4SDnwGkUzMoYAw" />
  </Fragment>

  <main class="site-about">
    <section class="about-hero" aria-labelledby="about-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">About Study Hub</p>
      <h1 id="about-title">A clearer route from finding a resource to understanding it.</h1>
      <p>Study Hub is an independent learning library built to help students explore subject materials, practise with exam resources, and study with more confidence.</p>
      <div class="about-hero-actions">
        <a class="about-primary-link" href={`${home}/subjects.html`}>Explore subjects <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a href={`${home}/documentation.html`}>How to use Study Hub</a>
      </div>
      <div class="about-hero-note">
        <span aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <p>Made for Ugandan learners, with a growing collection across secondary-school subjects.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section about-purpose" aria-labelledby="purpose-title">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The purpose</p>
        <h2 id="purpose-title">Make useful study material easier to navigate.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="about-section-copy">
        <p>Finding a good explanation or a relevant practice paper can take time. Study Hub brings subject pages, study notes, recent additions, and exam practice into one organised place so learners can spend more time learning and less time searching.</p>
        <p>The site is designed as a practical study companion, not a replacement for a teacher, a school syllabus, or an examining body. Students should use resources thoughtfully and confirm important requirements with their school.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section about-offerings" aria-labelledby="offerings-title">
      <div class="about-section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">What you can do</p>
        <h2 id="offerings-title">A study flow that stays connected.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="about-feature-grid">
        <article class="about-feature">
          <span class="about-feature-number">01</span>
          <h3>Start with a subject</h3>
          <p>Browse a subject directory and follow pages shaped around the topics and resources learners look for.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="about-feature">
          <span class="about-feature-number">02</span>
          <h3>Choose notes or practice</h3>
          <p>Explore notes and past papers, search the collection, and narrow results with the filters available on each page.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="about-feature">
          <span class="about-feature-number">03</span>
          <h3>Read at your pace</h3>
          <p>Open supported documents in a reader with page navigation, reading preferences, bookmarks, and related subject material.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="about-feature">
          <span class="about-feature-number">04</span>
          <h3>Ask for a clearer explanation</h3>
          <p>For PDFs, the optional AI study companion can explain visible page content. Its answers are suggestions to check, not official guidance.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section about-quality" aria-labelledby="quality-title">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">A growing library</p>
        <h2 id="quality-title">Useful materials need context and care.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="about-section-copy">
        <p>The library includes resources from different authors and sources. Titles and descriptions help students identify material, but a resource may be incomplete, outdated, or owned by someone else. Check the subject, level, and year where shown, and review a document before relying on it.</p>
        <p>Contributions are optional and reviewed before they can become part of the public collection. Contributors must have permission to share the material. If you notice an incorrect label, a broken file, or a rights concern, please contact Study Hub so it can be reviewed.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-contact" aria-labelledby="about-contact-title">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Keep improving the library</p>
        <h2 id="about-contact-title">Have a resource request or an idea?</h2>
        <p>Tell us what would make your study session more useful.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-contact-links">
        <a href={`${home}/community-chat.html`}>Share a suggestion <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a href={`${home}/library-guide.html`}>Read the Library Guide <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a href="mailto:trusteth777@gmail.com">Contact Study Hub <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
